+\reply
+We have added SQLRight as a baseline in RQ2. \TODO{supported target DBMSs, adaptation, campaign setting, and results of SQLRight}
+
+We have also extended the related work in Section~VI with sqllogictest and seed-selection techniques. sqllogictest validates query results across database engines with a shared test format, whereas \tool{} transfers test cases into seeds for coverage-guided fuzzing. Seed-selection and scheduling techniques, such as corpus minimization and power schedules (e.g., AFLFast), choose or prioritize seeds within an existing corpus, whereas \tool{} constructs the initial corpus for target DBMSs that lack one; the two directions are therefore orthogonal and can be combined.
+
+The updated Table~III and Table~IV with the SQLRight and SmartFuzz columns are shown in \metareviewref{3}.
 
